<zk>
	<label multiline="true">
		Steps to reproduce:
		1. Type "Sep 2, 2026" into begin, "Sep 4, 2025" into end (reversed), blur.

		- Expected: the errorbox names the reversed range AND both inputs still
			show what was typed, so the user can correct the year instead of
			retyping the pair.
		- Bug: the end input was wiped by the server snap-back, leaving an empty
			field plus an error about an entry no longer on screen.

		Guards, after step 1:
		- Correct the begin year to 2025 and blur: the pair on screen commits, so the
			label below the box shows an end value, not "none".
		- A redraw keeps both entries and the errorbox.

		2. Open the calendar and pick a later day first, then an earlier day.

		- Expected, changed by this ticket: the earlier second pick is NOT
			silently swapped into a valid range; it is rejected like a typed
			reversed pair, so both entry paths follow one rule.
	</label>
	<div>
		<daterangebox id="drb" format="MMM d, yyyy" numberOfMonths="2"
			onChange='var e = event.getEnd();
				committedEnd.setValue(e == null ? "none" : String.valueOf(e.getTime()));'/>
	</div>
	<label id="committedEnd"/>
</zk>
